<body>
<div class="author-tag">Javier Ramos Velasco &middot; Jos&eacute; Mar&iacute;a Serraclara</div>
<div class="deck">

<div class="slide active" data-slide="1">
  <div class="blob" style="width:520px;height:520px;top:-140px;right:-100px;background:#0369a1;opacity:.13"></div>
  <div class="blob" style="width:280px;height:280px;bottom:-90px;left:-60px;background:#1e3a5f;opacity:.09;animation-delay:5s"></div>
  <div class="content" style="text-align:center">
    <div class="reveal" style="display:inline-block;background:rgba(56,189,248,.08);border:1px solid rgba(56,189,248,.2);border-radius:40px;padding:.28rem 1.1rem;font-size:.68rem;letter-spacing:.13em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#38bdf8;margin-bottom:1.3rem">Non-Operating Owners &middot; The Capital Case</div>
    <h1 class="reveal" style="font-family:\'Playfair Display\',serif;font-size:clamp(1.9rem,4.5vw,3.7rem);font-weight:900;line-height:1.1;margin-bottom:1.1rem">The smartest money in shipping<br><span style="color:#38bdf8">doesn\'t move a single container.</span></h1>
    <p class="reveal" style="font-size:clamp(.85rem,1.2vw,.98rem);color:#94a3b8;max-width:680px;margin:0 auto 2rem;line-height:1.7">Non-Operating Owners control 35&ndash;40% of the global fleet by tonnage. They own the vessel, lease the earnings, and never touch the cargo. That separation of asset and operation is not a compromise &mdash; it is the model.</p>
    <div class="reveal" style="display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:2.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap">
      <div style="text-align:center"><div style="font-size:1.6rem;font-weight:800;color:#f1f5f9">35&ndash;40%</div><div class="label" style="color:var(--muted);margin-top:.15rem">Global fleet by tonnage</div></div>
      <div style="width:1px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.07)"></div>
      <div style="text-align:center"><div style="font-size:1.6rem;font-weight:800;color:#f59e0b">900k TEU</div><div class="label" style="color:var(--muted);margin-top:.15rem">Seaspan capacity alone</div></div>
      <div style="width:1px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.07)"></div>
      <div style="text-align:center"><div style="font-size:1.6rem;font-weight:800;color:#38bdf8">1&ndash;3 yr</div><div class="label" style="color:var(--muted);margin-top:.15rem">Typical time charter</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="slide" data-slide="2">
  <div class="blob" style="width:360px;height:360px;top:-80px;right:-80px;background:#0c4a6e;opacity:.1"></div>
  <div class="content">
    <div class="reveal label" style="color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:.3rem">The Ecosystem</div>
    <h2 class="reveal" style="font-family:\'Playfair Display\',serif;font-size:clamp(1.4rem,2.6vw,1.95rem);font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.3rem">Four players. One vessel. <span style="color:#38bdf8">None of them do the same job.</span></h2>
    <p class="reveal" style="font-size:.83rem;color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.6;max-width:740px;margin-bottom:1rem">Shipping looks like one industry from the outside. From the inside, it is at least four different businesses sharing the same steel hull.</p>
    <div class="reveal" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:.75rem;margin-bottom:1rem">
      <div style="border-radius:14px;padding:1rem;border:1px solid rgba(56,189,248,.25);background:rgba(56,189,248,.04)">
        <div style="font-size:.6rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#38bdf8;margin-bottom:.4rem">NOO</div>
        <div style="font-size:.95rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.35rem">Asset Owner</div>
        <div class="mini">Owns the vessel. Earns charter hire. Bears residual value risk. Does not operate.</div>
        <div style="margin-top:.55rem;font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;color:#38bdf8">&larr; This is the investment</div>
      </div>
      <div style="border-radius:14px;padding:1rem;border:1px solid rgba(245,158,11,.2);background:rgba(245,158,11,.03)">
        <div style="font-size:.6rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#f59e0b;margin-bottom:.4rem">Carrier</div>
        <div style="font-size:.95rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.35rem">Operator</div>
        <div class="mini">Charters the vessel. Runs the route. Manages bunkers, port calls, crew. Pays hire daily.</div>
        <div style="margin-top:.55rem;font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;color:#f59e0b">MSC &middot; Maersk &middot; CMA CGM</div>
      </div>
      <div style="border-radius:14px;padding:1rem;border:1px solid rgba(167,139,250,.2);background:rgba(167,139,250,.03)">
        <div style="font-size:.6rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#a78bfa;margin-bottom:.4rem">Shipper</div>
        <div style="font-size:.95rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.35rem">Cargo Owner</div>
        <div class="mini">Books space on the vessel. Pays freight rate. Relationship is with the carrier, not the NOO.</div>
        <div style="margin-top:.55rem;font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;color:#a78bfa">Retailers &middot; Manufacturers</div>
      </div>
      <div style="border-radius:14px;padding:1rem;border:1px solid rgba(74,222,128,.2);background:rgba(74,222,128,.03)">
        <div style="font-size:.6rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#4ade80;margin-bottom:.4rem">Capital</div>
        <div style="font-size:.95rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.35rem">Debt / Equity</div>
        <div class="mini">Finances the acquisition. Charter contract is the collateral. NOO is the credit story.</div>
        <div style="margin-top:.55rem;font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;color:#4ade80">Banks &middot; Bonds &middot; Ship finance</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal" style="padding:.75rem 1rem;border-radius:10px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.025);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.06);font-size:.8rem;color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.55">
      <span style="color:#38bdf8;font-weight:700">The NOO insight:</span> The asset owner sits between capital markets and the operating world, earning a spread. The vessel is the collateral. The charter is the income statement. The residual is the upside.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="slide" data-slide="3">
  <div class="blob" style="width:400px;height:400px;top:-100px;right:-80px;background:#1e3a5f;opacity:.1"></div>
  <div class="blob" style="width:250px;height:250px;bottom:-70px;left:-50px;background:#0369a1;opacity:.08;animation-delay:6s"></div>
  <div class="content">
    <div class="reveal label" style="color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:.3rem">Investment Flow</div>
    <h2 class="reveal" style="font-family:\'Playfair Display\',serif;font-size:clamp(1.4rem,2.6vw,1.95rem);font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.25rem">Buy the asset. <span style="color:#4ade80">Lease the earnings.</span> Sell at the cycle.</h2>
    <p class="reveal" style="font-size:.82rem;color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.6;max-width:760px;margin-bottom:.85rem">The NOO model is simple in principle. The edge comes from execution &mdash; timing the acquisition, locking the charter, and reading the residual correctly.</p>
    <div class="flow-wrap reveal">
      <div class="flow-node">
        <div class="flow-box" style="border-color:rgba(56,189,248,.3);background:rgba(56,189,248,.06)">
          <div style="font-size:.55rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#38bdf8;margin-bottom:.3rem">01</div>
          <div class="flow-num" style="color:#38bdf8">Acquire</div>
          <div class="flow-label">Vessel purchase</div>
          <div class="flow-sub">Newbuild or S&amp;P<br>Debt + equity</div>
          <div class="flow-pill p-blue">Capital deployed</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</div>
      <div class="flow-node">
        <div class="flow-box" style="border-color:rgba(245,158,11,.3);background:rgba(245,158,11,.05)">
          <div style="font-size:.55rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#f59e0b;margin-bottom:.3rem">02</div>
          <div class="flow-num" style="color:#f59e0b">Charter</div>
          <div class="flow-label">Time charter out</div>
          <div class="flow-sub">1&ndash;3 yr contract<br>Daily hire locked</div>
          <div class="flow-pill p-neu">Cash flow secured</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</div>
      <div class="flow-node">
        <div class="flow-box" style="border-color:rgba(74,222,128,.3);background:rgba(74,222,128,.05)">
          <div style="font-size:.55rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#4ade80;margin-bottom:.3rem">03</div>
          <div class="flow-num" style="color:#4ade80">Earn</div>
          <div class="flow-label">Carrier pays daily</div>
          <div class="flow-sub">Service debt<br>Distribute free cash</div>
          <div class="flow-pill p-pos">Predictable yield</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</div>
      <div class="flow-node">
        <div class="flow-box" style="border-color:rgba(167,139,250,.3);background:rgba(167,139,250,.05)">
          <div style="font-size:.55rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#a78bfa;margin-bottom:.3rem">04</div>
          <div class="flow-num" style="color:#a78bfa">Re-rate</div>
          <div class="flow-label">Charter renewal</div>
          <div class="flow-sub">Refix at higher rate<br>or extend</div>
          <div class="flow-pill" style="background:rgba(167,139,250,.12);color:#a78bfa">Rate upside</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</div>
      <div class="flow-node">
        <div class="flow-box" style="border-color:rgba(248,113,113,.3);background:rgba(248,113,113,.05)">
          <div style="font-size:.55rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#f87171;margin-bottom:.3rem">05</div>
          <div class="flow-num" style="color:#f87171">Exit</div>
          <div class="flow-label">Vessel sale</div>
          <div class="flow-sub">Cycle peak or<br>scrap value</div>
          <div class="flow-pill p-neg">Residual capture</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:.7rem;margin-top:.85rem">
      <div style="padding:.65rem .9rem;border-radius:9px;background:rgba(56,189,248,.05);border:1px solid rgba(56,189,248,.12)">
        <div style="font-size:.7rem;font-weight:700;color:#38bdf8;margin-bottom:.2rem">The collateral logic</div>
        <div class="mini">The vessel is the asset. The charter is the cash flow. Together they are a financeable credit story.</div>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:.65rem .9rem;border-radius:9px;background:rgba(74,222,128,.05);border:1px solid rgba(74,222,128,.12)">
        <div style="font-size:.7rem;font-weight:700;color:#4ade80;margin-bottom:.2rem">Where alpha lives</div>
        <div class="mini">Buying in down-cycle. Locking long charters at the inflection. Residual is the return enhancer.</div>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:.65rem .9rem;border-radius:9px;background:rgba(248,113,113,.05);border:1px solid rgba(248,113,113,.12)">
        <div style="font-size:.7rem;font-weight:700;color:#f87171;margin-bottom:.2rem">The real risk</div>
        <div class="mini">Residual value at exit. Charter counterparty credit. Obsolescence from EEXI / CII regulation.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="slide" data-slide="4">
  <div class="blob" style="width:380px;height:380px;top:-90px;right:-70px;background:#0c4a6e;opacity:.1"></div>
  <div class="content">
    <div class="reveal label" style="color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:.3rem">Two Business Models</div>
    <h2 class="reveal" style="font-family:\'Playfair Display\',serif;font-size:clamp(1.4rem,2.6vw,1.95rem);font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.25rem">Same vessel. <span style="color:#38bdf8">Completely different game.</span></h2>
    <p class="reveal" style="font-size:.82rem;color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.6;max-width:740px;margin-bottom:.8rem">Carriers and NOOs share the same asset class but operate on different risk surfaces. That split is where the investable edge lives.</p>
    <div class="vs-grid reveal">
      <div class="vs-col">
        <span class="vs-label" style="background:rgba(245,158,11,.1);color:#f59e0b">Carrier &middot; Operator logic</span>
        <div class="vs-row"><span style="color:#f59e0b;font-weight:700">Revenue:</span> Freight rates &mdash; volatile, demand-driven</div>
        <div class="vs-row"><span style="color:#f59e0b;font-weight:700">Cost base:</span> Fuel, port, crew, hire &mdash; all variable</div>
        <div class="vs-row"><span style="color:#f59e0b;font-weight:700">Asset stance:</span> Fleet as a capacity tool, not an investment</div>
        <div class="vs-row"><span style="color:#f59e0b;font-weight:700">Capital:</span> Freed for route &amp; network expansion</div>
        <div class="vs-row"><span style="color:#f59e0b;font-weight:700">Cycle:</span> Full exposure &mdash; top and bottom</div>
        <div class="vs-row" style="border-color:rgba(245,158,11,.2)"><span style="color:#f59e0b;font-weight:700">Edge:</span> Scale, customers, logistics integration</div>
      </div>
      <div class="vs-divider">
        <div class="vs-dot"></div><div class="vs-dot"></div><div class="vs-dot"></div>
        <div style="font-size:.75rem;font-weight:800;color:rgba(255,255,255,.12);writing-mode:vertical-rl;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;transform:rotate(180deg)">vs</div>
        <div class="vs-dot"></div><div class="vs-dot"></div><div class="vs-dot"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="vs-col">
        <span class="vs-label" style="background:rgba(56,189,248,.1);color:#38bdf8">NOO &middot; Asset-owner logic</span>
        <div class="vs-row"><span style="color:#38bdf8;font-weight:700">Revenue:</span> Charter hire &mdash; contracted, predictable</div>
        <div class="vs-row"><span style="color:#38bdf8;font-weight:700">Cost base:</span> Dry-dock, insurance, finance &mdash; manageable</div>
        <div class="vs-row"><span style="color:#38bdf8;font-weight:700">Asset stance:</span> Vessel is the core investment</div>
        <div class="vs-row"><span style="color:#38bdf8;font-weight:700">Capital:</span> Leveraged acquisition &mdash; balance sheet is the business</div>
        <div class="vs-row"><span style="color:#38bdf8;font-weight:700">Cycle:</span> Managed &mdash; risk isolated to re-charter windows</div>
        <div class="vs-row" style="border-color:rgba(56,189,248,.2)"><span style="color:#38bdf8;font-weight:700">Edge:</span> Fleet timing, charter execution, residual discipline</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="slide" data-slide="5">
  <div class="blob" style="width:350px;height:350px;top:-80px;right:-70px;background:#1e3a5f;opacity:.1"></div>
  <div class="blob" style="width:220px;height:220px;bottom:-60px;left:-40px;background:#0369a1;opacity:.07;animation-delay:7s"></div>
  <div class="content">
    <div class="reveal label" style="color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:.3rem">Why This Matters Now</div>
    <h2 class="reveal" style="font-family:\'Playfair Display\',serif;font-size:clamp(1.4rem,2.6vw,1.95rem);font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.75rem">Four structural forces are making the NOO model <span style="color:#4ade80">more relevant, not less.</span></h2>
    <div class="reveal" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:.75rem;margin-bottom:1rem">
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-val" style="color:#38bdf8">+22%</div>
        <div class="stat-lbl">Charter rates YoY</div>
        <div class="stat-note">Container segment, 2024&ndash;25</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-val" style="color:#4ade80">~40%</div>
        <div class="stat-lbl">Fleet chartered in</div>
        <div class="stat-note">Even MSC and Maersk</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-val" style="color:#f59e0b">900k</div>
        <div class="stat-lbl">TEU Seaspan</div>
        <div class="stat-note">One NOO, global scale</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-val" style="color:#f87171">2027</div>
        <div class="stat-lbl">EEXI / CII tightening</div>
        <div class="stat-note">Older tonnage at risk</div>
      </div>
